Package: MkPrime
Title: Bayesian Phylogenetic Inference Under the Mk' Model
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Martin R.", "Smith", email = "martin.smith@durham.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5660-1727")),
    person("Andrew F.", "Magee", role = "ctb",
           comment = c("Fréchet correlation ESS and pseudo-ESS methods (treess package)",
                        ORCID = "0000-0001-8831-6226"))
  )
Description: Bayesian inference of phylogenetic trees from discrete
    morphological characters under the Mk' (Mk-prime) model, which infers
    the true number of character states including those not observed in the
    data. Supports three character types in a single analysis: asymmetric
    binary (neomorphic), Mk' with inferred state count (transformational),
    and standard Mk with known state space. Implements Markov chain Monte
    Carlo with parallel tempering, among-character rate variation, and
    ascertainment bias correction.
